WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.070
Ice sheets spread, then
melted back, again and again,

2
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:06.830
for millions of years before humans.

3
00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:09.070
Something flipped the switch.

4
00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.670
Suspect one: volcanoes.

5
00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:17.050
Large explosive eruptions inject sulfur
dioxide high into the stratosphere.

6
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:23.970
Suspect two: between 1645 and
1715, the Sun showed few sunspots.

7
00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:27.870
Suspect three: about 34 million years ago,

8
00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.810
Antarctica was rapidly buried in ice.

9
00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:33.690
So what switched the ice ages on and off?

10
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:34.830
The Sun?

11
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:35.770
Volcanoes?

12
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.150
Drifting continents?

13
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.290
Something else?

14
00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:42.610
In this mission, you'll meet four
natural drivers of climate change.

15
00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.490
Then you'll weigh how big
each driver's effect is,

16
00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:48.270
and whether any of them
explains today's warming.

17
00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:53.390
Your mission: find out what
switched the ice ages on and off.
